From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Petersen <ispeters@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 5 Sep 2026 12:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] diag: classify the bytes of arrays actually read in the window

Not for upstream.  Instrumentation only.  Applies on top of 0005.

0005 established that this TU enters the window 16 times per compile, for
16 distinct decls, all with NumTemplateArgs == 2, and that the caller is
the same every time: getFunctionTypeInternal -> FunctionProtoType::Profile
-> Stmt::Profile -> StmtProfiler::VisitConceptSpecializationExpr.

A crash needs three things at once: the window is entered, the slab
backing that decl holds recycled bytes rather than fresh zeroed pages,
and those bytes are fatal rather than merely wrong.  The first conjunct
is now measured and is identical (16) at stock,
CLANG_CONSTRAINT_CACHE_RESERVE=3071 and =3072, so the reserve knob's
suppression does not act there.  The census patch (0004) measured the
second conjunct over the wrong population -- all 539 decls at creation,
almost all of which are written promptly and never read in the window --
and found ~45% garbage in both the crashing and non-crashing arms.

This patch measures the second conjunct over the right population: the
bytes of the trailing array at the moment it is read, for exactly those
16 arrays.  Each read is classified zero / aa / 55 / mixed, the counts
are reported in the exit summary, and the first bytes are dumped for
mixed arrays.

The prediction under the surviving hypothesis is that stock shows mixed
arrays among the 16 and reserve(3072) shows zero.  If both arms look the
same, the reserve effect is in none of the three conjuncts we have
enumerated, and it should be reported upstream as an unexplained
observation rather than explained away for a third time.

Note the counters are tallied regardless of CLANG_ICS_WINDOW_LINES, so
the rate arms can run with LINES=0 and STACKS=0 and still report.

NOTE: paths in this diff are relative to the `clang/` subdirectory of the
llvm-project monorepo, to match this repo's clang derivation's sourceRoot
(clang-src-.../clang).
---
--- a/lib/AST/DeclTemplate.cpp
+++ b/lib/AST/DeclTemplate.cpp
@@ -1145,6 +1145,7 @@
 #include "llvm/Support/Signals.h"
 #include "llvm/Support/raw_ostream.h"
 #include <cstdlib>
+#include <cstring>
 
 namespace {
 struct ICSWindowProbe {
@@ -1152,6 +1153,7 @@
   unsigned StackBudget = 3;
   unsigned LineBudget = 50;
   unsigned long Reads = 0;
+  unsigned long Zero = 0, AA = 0, Fill55 = 0, Mixed = 0;
   llvm::SmallPtrSet<const void *, 16> Decls;
 
   ICSWindowProbe() {
@@ -1166,7 +1168,9 @@
   ~ICSWindowProbe() {
     if (Enabled)
       llvm::errs() << "[ics-window] in-window-reads=" << Reads
-                   << " distinct-decls=" << Decls.size() << "\n";
+                   << " distinct-decls=" << Decls.size() << " zero=" << Zero
+                   << " aa=" << AA << " 55=" << Fill55 << " mixed=" << Mixed
+                   << "\n";
   }
 };
 
@@ -1184,11 +1188,52 @@
   ++P.Reads;
   bool First = P.Decls.insert(this).second;
 
+  // Classify the bytes of *this* array -- the population that matters.  The
+  // census patch (0004) samples every decl at creation, which is dominated by
+  // arrays that are written promptly and never read in the window; only these
+  // reads can produce a crash, and only if the bytes happen to be fatal rather
+  // than merely wrong.  Byte-at-a-time memcpy for the same reason as 0004.
+  const auto *Bytes =
+      reinterpret_cast<const unsigned char *>(getTrailingObjects());
+  const size_t NumBytes = size_t(NumTemplateArgs) * sizeof(TemplateArgument);
+  bool AllZero = true, AllAA = true, All55 = true;
+  for (size_t I = 0; I != NumBytes; ++I) {
+    unsigned char B;
+    std::memcpy(&B, Bytes + I, 1);
+    AllZero &= (B == 0x00);
+    AllAA &= (B == 0xAA);
+    All55 &= (B == 0x55);
+  }
+  const char *Class = "mixed";
+  if (!NumBytes)
+    Class = "empty";
+  else if (AllZero) {
+    Class = "zero";
+    ++P.Zero;
+  } else if (AllAA) {
+    Class = "aa";
+    ++P.AA;
+  } else if (All55) {
+    Class = "55";
+    ++P.Fill55;
+  } else
+    ++P.Mixed;
+
   if (P.LineBudget) {
     --P.LineBudget;
     llvm::errs() << "[ics-window] read decl=" << (const void *)this
                  << " nargs=" << NumTemplateArgs << (First ? " first" : "")
-                 << "\n";
+                 << " bytes=" << Class;
+    if (NumBytes && !AllZero && !AllAA && !All55) {
+      static const char Hex[] = "0123456789abcdef";
+      llvm::errs() << " raw=";
+      for (size_t I = 0; I != (NumBytes < 24 ? NumBytes : size_t(24)); ++I) {
+        unsigned char B;
+        std::memcpy(&B, Bytes + I, 1);
+        llvm::errs() << Hex[B >> 4] << Hex[B & 0xf];
+      }
+    }
+    llvm::errs() << "\n";
   }
 
   if (First && P.StackBudget) {
-- 
